2. THE ASSEMBLER (60 Percent Category)
- Implements two-pass assembly using an in-memory intermediate representation.
- Diagnoses and logs label errors:
  * Duplicate label definitions
  * Invalid label names starting with digits
  * Undefined labels and forward references
  * Warnings for unused labels and potential infinite loops
- Generates 32-bit little-endian binary object files (.o).
- Suppresses object file generation if errors are found.
- Generates formatted program listing files (.lst) with inline error notes.
- Generates assembly log files (.log) with full symbol table dumps.
- Implements table-driven instruction lookup.
- Supports pseudo-instructions:
  * data value (reserves 32-bit word in memory and increments PC)
  * SET value (binds constant value to label without advancing PC)
- Supports arithmetic extension instructions:
  * mul (opcode 19)
  * div (opcode 20)

3. THE EMULATOR (25 Percent Category)
- Loads and executes 32-bit binary object files (.o).
- Implements all four registers: Accumulator (A), Secondary (B), Program Counter (PC), and Stack Pointer (SP).
- Implements implicit PC pre-increment on instruction fetch.
- Supports all 21 ISA instructions:
  ldc, adc, ldl, stl, ldnl, stnl, add, sub, shl, shr, adj, a2sp, sp2a, call, return, brz, brlz, br, HALT, mul, div.
- Command-line execution flags:
  * -trace: Step-by-step register and instruction trace
  * -before: Hexadecimal memory dump before execution
  * -after: Hexadecimal memory dump after execution
  * -isa: Complete instruction set reference table
- Safety traps and error detection:
  * Division by zero runtime trap on div instruction (halts with diagnostic message)
  * Memory boundary / segmentation bounds checking
  * Unknown opcode traps
  * Infinite runaway execution cycle guard (MAX_CYCLES)

